<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady in limited trade.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady in limited trade.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets in limited trade on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices fell by 200 rupees per tonne on increased selling from processing plants and refineries on little trading. activity.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in thin trade. Soymeal yellow was $281-282 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,350 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,300 rupees FOR Bhavnagar. Business volumes were low.</p>
